= Ajay U. Mandlekar -- Teaching
[https://ee.stanford.edu Department of Electrical Engineering], [https://stanford.edu Stanford University]

I have had the good fortune of helping teach some of my favorite classes at both Stanford and Caltech. I love teaching and hope to continue spreading knowledge about stuff that interests me. 

== Stanford

- CS 231N: [http://cs231n.stanford.edu/ Convolutional Neural Networks for Visual Recognition]
-- Instructors: [http://vision.stanford.edu/feifeili/ Fei-Fei Li], [http://cs.stanford.edu/people/jcjohns/ Justin Johnson], [http://ai.stanford.edu/~syyeung/ Serena Yeung]
-- Teaching Assistant for Spring 2018

- CS 332: [http://cs332.stanford.edu/\#!index.md Advanced Survey of Reinforcement Learning] 
-- Instructors: [http://cs.stanford.edu/people/ebrun/ Emma Brunskill], [http://ai.stanford.edu/~garg/ Animesh Garg]
-- Teaching Assistant for Fall 2017

== Caltech

- ACM 95ab: [http://www.piercelab.caltech.edu/people/niles/teaching/acm95a Introductory Methods of Applied Mathematics for the Physical Sciences] 
-- Instructors: [http://www.piercelab.caltech.edu/people/niles Niles Pierce], [http://www.cms.caltech.edu/people/dim Dan Meiron]
-- Teaching Assistant for Winter 2016 and Spring 2016
-- Although not directly related to my research, I had a great time being a TA for these classes. [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Complex_analysis Complex Analysis] is an extremely fascinating branch of mathematics that has several unexpected results and applications. Studying ODEs and transforms has also helped me with understanding some techniques used in optimal control. 

- CS 24: [http://courses.cms.caltech.edu/cs24/lectures/ Introduction to Computing Systems] 
-- Instructor: [http://users.cms.caltech.edu/~donnie/ Donnie Pinkston]
-- Teaching Assistant for Spring 2015
